{"url": "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/application-guide/declaration-and-payment/application-fee-waivers", "final_url": "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/application-guide/declaration-and-payment/application-fee-waivers", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-30", "text": "Your choice regarding cookies on this site\nEssential cookies are enabled by default to give you the best possible site experience. For details on the other cookies we use click on settings, or accept them all.\nAccept allI do not acceptSettings\nSkip to main content\nSupplementary navigation\nAdmissions\nNews\nResearch\nSearch\nMain navigation\nMenu\nYou are here:\nHome\nAdmissions\nGraduate\nApplication Guide\nDeclaration and payment\nApplication fee waivers\nApplication fee waivers\nInformation on application fee waiver schemes and their eligibility criteria.\nThe tower at Christ Church. Credit: Yixing Wu / Graduate Photography Competition\nShow contents\nApplying from a low-income country\nRefugees and displaced persons\nUK applicants from low-income backgrounds\nUNIQplus applicants\nApplying for readmission\nApplying to closely related research courses\nShow contents\nYou are reading:\nApplying from a low-income country\nRefugees and displaced persons\nUK applicants from low-income backgrounds\nUNIQplus applicants\nApplying for readmission\nApplying to closely related research courses\nApplying from a low-income country\nExpand all\nIf you indicate on the application form that you are resident in one of the eligible countries in this section of the guidance, you will be asked additional questions relating to this waiver scheme. If your answers to these questions indicate that you are eligible for this waiver, you will not be directed to the payment screens when you submit your application.\nEligibility\nCountries eligible for this application fee waiver\nRefugees and displaced persons\nIf you are, or were, a refugee; stateless person; asylum seeker; or have been otherwise forcibly displaced within or outside your country of origin, you are eligible for an application fee waiver as long as you meet the minimum entry requirements for the course.\nTo request this waiver, answer \u2018yes\u2019 to the appropriate question on the \u2018About You\u2019 tab of the application form.\nUK applicants from low-income backgrounds\nExpand all\nSome UK applicants from low-income backgrounds are eligible for a fee waiver.\nEligibility\nEngland\nNorthern Ireland\nScotland\nWales\nUK applicants in receipt of UK Government benefits\nHow to request a UK low-income application fee waiver\nWhen to request it\nUNIQplus applicants\nExpand all\nApplicants who applied to UNIQplus at the University of Oxford and met the eligibility criteria can request that the graduate application fee be waived.\nHow to request a UNIQplus fee waiver\nWhen to request it\nApplying for readmission\nIf you are currently studying for an Oxford graduate taught course and applying for a research course with no break in your studies, you may be eligible to apply for readmission. You must meet the same deadlines and requirements as other applicants, but you won't be required to pay an application fee. Find more information about readmissions status in this Application Guide.\nApplying to closely related research courses\nExpand all\nIf you apply to one of c.20 Centres for Doctoral Training (CDT) courses or DPhils that are similarly structured, you may apply for two additional eligible courses and pay only one application fee.\nEligibility criteria for your first course application\nEligibility criteria for additional courses\nHow to find an eligible additional course in the Medical Sciences Division\nHow to find an eligible additional course in the MPLS Division\nHow to request a waiver\nAny questions?\nTry our database of FAQs or submit your own question.\nView our FAQs\nDeclaration and payment\nContinue your application\nSubmitting your application\nThe pre-submission checklist, guidance on how to submit your application, and what happens after you have submitted your application.\nApplication fee\nGuidance on paying the application fee.\nWas this page helpful?\nYes, it was\nNo, it wasn't\nInformation about\nOxford University\nStrategic plan\nOxford's research\nCourse fees and funding\nLibraries\nMuseums and collections\nOpen days\nOxford glossary\nEquality policy\nFreedom of speech statement\nStatement on modern slavery\nData protection / UK GDPR\nSport\nConferences at Oxford\nInformation for\nProspective undergraduates\nUndergraduate applicant privacy policy\nUndergraduate outreach privacy policy\nProspective graduate students\nPostgraduate applicant privacy policy\nProspective Lifelong Learning students\nProspective online/distance learning students\nCurrent Oxford students\nCurrent Oxford staff\nVisitors/Tourists\nMedia\nAlumni\nTeachers\nBusinesses/Partnerships\nQuick links\nAny questions?\nJobs and vacancies\nTerm dates\nMap\nAccess Guide\nNexus365 email\nGiving to Oxford\nContact us\nLegal\nWebsite privacy policy\nAccessibility statement\nCookie settings\nConnect with us\nYouTube\nX\nFacebook\nTikTok\nLinkedIn\nWeibo\nInstagram\nMedium\nThe Conversation\nBluesky\n\u00a9 2026 University of Oxford", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/application-guide/declaration-and-payment/application-fee-waivers#main-content"], ["", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/"], ["Admissions", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions"], ["News", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/news"], ["Research", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/research"], ["Site search", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/search"], ["Undergraduate courses", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate/courses/course-listing"], ["Graduate courses", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/graduate/courses/find-your-course"], ["Admissions", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/undergraduate"], ["Undergraduate", "https://www.ox.ac.uk/admissions/